  "id": "DrugBank_DB09074 - MONDO_3792",
  "verbalization": "Olaparib is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ovarian Carcinosarcoma through a series of interconnected indications. The drug is linked to Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary, which in turn is associated with Melphalan and Rucaparib, both of which are indicated for Ovarian Carcinosarcoma. This suggests a potential pathway where Olaparib may exert its effects through a mechanism that is shared with other drugs in the same class, such as Rucaparib, which also targets Ovarian Carcinosarcoma. The presence of multiple indications pointing to Ovarian Carcinosarcoma from different entities, including Melphalan and Rucaparib, indicates that Olaparib may have a role in the treatment of this cancer, possibly through mechanisms that are not yet fully understood. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on certain chemotherapy agents, which may be part of a broader therapeutic strategy for this disease.",
